# TASK-QA-010/OPS-001/OPS-008 finding: these three scripts are genuine CI
# dependencies -- release.yml runs security_hardening_check.sh and
# notarize.sh on every tagged release push, ci.yml runs
# verify_acceptance_criteria.py on every push/PR -- unlike the rest of
# /scripts/ (local-only dev tooling: DMG signing prep, backup/restore,
# rollback, that needs local credentials/interactive input CI never has).
# All three were previously gitignored along with everything else in this
# directory, meaning release.yml would have failed with "file not found" on
# the very first real tagged release (neither script has ever actually been
# in the repository despite being referenced by a workflow the whole time).
# Git can't re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded via a
# trailing-slash pattern (`/scripts/`), hence `/scripts/*` here instead --
# the standard "ignore all but these" idiom.
!/scripts/verify_acceptance_criteria.py
!/scripts/security_hardening_check.sh
!/scripts/notarize.sh
!/scripts/verify_release_prerequisites.sh
!/scripts/generate_release_notes.sh
!/scripts/.placeholder_license_public.pem.sha256
audit.md
fix-log.md
implementation-log.md
README.md
/docs/